course: dictionary
lesson: 5286
title: One word, many jumps
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word jump can mean different things, so context tells you which meaning to use. Jump can mean pushing yourself into the air with your legs, moving suddenly because you are surprised, or rising quickly, like a price or a number. Read the words around it, then ask which meaning fits.
explain: «Blowing too hard makes a recorder jump up to a shrill squeal.» The recorder does not leave the table, so jump here means rise suddenly, to a higher sound. A soft, steady breath gives a clear note instead. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it: "rise suddenly to a high squeal" makes sense.
explain: Jump is also a noun. A jump is one push into the air, or the distance of that push. In a jumping contest, the jumps are measured in inches or metres, and the longest jump wins. Phrases such as «jump rope» and «jump the queue» have their own meanings, so learn them as whole chunks.
fact: Jump can be a verb (jump, jumps, jumped, jumping) or a noun (a jump, jumps).
fact: To jump means to push yourself up or forward into the air with your legs.
fact: To jump can also mean to move suddenly because you are surprised or scared, or to rise suddenly, like a price or a number.
fact: «Jumping merrily along hand in hand, in couples» describes children skipping happily, pushing off the ground with each step.
fact: On a number line, jumps of equal size show adding or counting in steps: jumps of 2 land on 2, 4, 6 and so on.
exercise: «Blowing too hard makes a recorder jump up to a shrill squeal.» What does jump mean here? | Count to ten | Sit down quietly | *Rise suddenly to a high sound | Fall to the floor
exercise: The children went «jumping merrily along hand in hand, in couples». What were they doing? | Standing very still | Counting coins | *Skipping along with happy hops | Sleeping in a line
exercise: Someone «jumps the queue». What have they done? | Left the shop early | Asked for a drink | *Pushed in front of people who were waiting | Counted the people
test: Sam did ten rope jumps. What is one rope jump? | A slow walk along a path | *One push into the air over a turning rope | A knot in the rope | A rope bought from a shop
test: On a number line, jumps of 2 show what? | *Counting or adding in equal steps | Stopping at every number | Running backwards | Drawing a circle
exam: «The price began to jump after the storm.» What does jump mean? | Sing loudly | Stay exactly the same | Fall into a hole | *Rise suddenly
